      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I am deeply sorry that you feel this profound sense of hopelessness and that the \"nothing left\" feeling is so overwhelming. Please know that these thoughts of hopelessness and self-lessness are common during the acute grief phase when the brain cannot process the sudden end of a 25-year life. If these feelings of emptiness feel too heavy to carry alone, please consider reaching out to a crisis helpline or a trusted support group to help you find a safe way to stay.",
