      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear the devastating finality you feel when the \"logic\" of 25 years is shatterd, and I want you to know that feeling like a \"dead\" or \"hollow\" self is a normal part of the grief process where the \"you\" who was the caretaker no longer exists. Please be gentle with yourself as you mourn the death of that entire life, not to be forceful to \"build something new\" when you feel you cannot; those later \"you's\" will not find the meaning you are seeking now. I encourage you to share this feeling with a therapist who can help you navigate this painful \"death\" of the self so you do not end alone.",
